{"event_type":"review","id":"69da958f41b062c1f9c40149128fa932b5c6cea6865644e9daad44be75417917","occurred_at":"2026-11-13T20:21:30Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/530facde595d0690bac3d6314f4c909088d0e29e8e519f1689ee4ededcc3f903","sha256":"530facde595d0690bac3d6314f4c909088d0e29e8e519f1689ee4ededcc3f903"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/aa2abd7182cb7c69752aad2e1e7f765b3db1da45291b7a3cb1d456bb598d1c60","sha256":"aa2abd7182cb7c69752aad2e1e7f765b3db1da45291b7a3cb1d456bb598d1c60"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/67f17be279ce5955916bf9df71a272326f6143fd64ff97706f4a1695be524d8c","sha256":"67f17be279ce5955916bf9df71a272326f6143fd64ff97706f4a1695be524d8c"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3ee8658a2643586210200cba5ae4db515f8ef94860620385ae2f54bdf515fe95","sha256":"3ee8658a2643586210200cba5ae4db515f8ef94860620385ae2f54bdf515fe95"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6c4b8b5a0279cb97efcd712d63637654497b9b107342ffd3f4a479e5438bfbb2","sha256":"6c4b8b5a0279cb97efcd712d63637654497b9b107342ffd3f4a479e5438bfbb2"}],"attempt_id":"5e1ccd3c03b0c11de50a6196fb050e14707115bd1d581473e0c1965d70a66654:0:1","base":"6a86582fbb554b0c10afb7210085e391bfcec38b","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"7dd72aa97d9f4266f605f096a689a290679601be","body":"**Check guest confinement before dispatching every phase.**\n\nRunning `vm-unit-switch-guest.py activators-positive` outside the disposable guest reaches `repair_clean()` (Line 2036) before any hostname or baseline check. That function stops `crq-repair.service`, `crq-repair.timer`, and `crq-repair.path`. On an account with production units, this stops the production repair scheduler even when fixture preparation never ran.\n\nMove the existing disposable-guest checks into `main()` before phase dispatch. The checks in `phase_prepare()` and `activators_install()` do not protect the other phases.","id":"c8206a5ec2d4f165c432e9e58d2dc37e19b0cd7369c16f61743b87b7d0411769","intervals":[[2659,2659]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-unit-switch-guest.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Check guest confinement before dispatching every phase."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"1cc517bee77846e4653e716df11877c87cd16ee6","body":"**Require complete identities before proving lifecycle changes.**\n\nIf `manager_restart.before.manager` is missing, both comparisons against the recorded after-identity can still pass because `None` differs from its PID and invocation ID. Likewise, a missing `boot_id_before` passes when `boot_id_after` is non-empty. Recomputed checks can therefore accept incomplete boundary evidence.\n\nRequire positive PIDs and non-empty invocation and boot IDs on both sides before comparing them.","id":"8b37cfbfd0f905dfa57c460ca08319ebd6a97b29ff40b76a431373db6df00081","intervals":[[965,972]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-feasibility.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Require complete identities before proving lifecycle changes."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"1cc517bee77846e4653e716df11877c87cd16ee6","body":"**Verify the run-log prefix before extracting new records.**\n\nLine 997 treats equal or greater length as proof of log continuity. If `before_runs` contains record A and `after_runs` contains a different record B at the same length, `new_runs` becomes empty. Both the observation check and `no_new_service_after_*` then pass, even when B records a new service execution.\n\nRequire `after_runs[:len(before_runs)] == before_runs`. Treat a changed or truncated prefix as non-passing evidence.","id":"769c56ebe36bca251354e06f7c6eab6277720a0d7e94a6211f08b1093f174dbf","intervals":[[997,998]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-feasibility.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Verify the run-log prefix before extracting new records."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"1cc517bee77846e4653e716df11877c87cd16ee6","body":"**Preserve the I1 error contract at the CLI boundary.**\n\nIf `run` lacks `--source-commit`, this handler emits no JSON artifact. If a guest phase raises `RuntimeError`, this handler also returns argument-error exit code 2 instead of runtime-error exit code 1. The parser additionally rejects `--json`, so callers cannot request the required machine-mode behavior.\n\nRoute parsing and operation failures through structured JSON error handling. Keep stderr empty in machine mode and distinguish usage errors from runtime errors.\n\nAs per coding guidelines, “Every operation invocation writes machine-readable JSON to stdout” and exit codes distinguish “1 thrown error” from “2 arg error.”","id":"44b15bc92276d820a7b43761c2fbe0ae743effa99a5ce77fa0c1eaf643a45f27","intervals":[[1345,1347]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-feasibility.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Preserve the I1 error contract at the CLI boundary."}],"head":"ecef30c961343d439a1206ad8cd70f203b46c8a5","head_tree":"7e3bc6040d8da1acb2564424b853efe795537180","input_scope":[{"blob":"a3d0a4e35ed46af3d0c64f5133f649d91f55d3fa","intervals":[[1,74]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/unit-switch-fixture.py"},{"blob":"1cc517bee77846e4653e716df11877c87cd16ee6","intervals":[[1,1351]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-feasibility.py"},{"blob":"33546bd986bc4915084687d7393b759b9057319d","intervals":[[1,520]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-guest-probe.py"},{"blob":"7dd72aa97d9f4266f605f096a689a290679601be","intervals":[[1,2728]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-unit-switch-guest.py"}],"job_id":"5e1ccd3c03b0c11de50a6196fb050e14707115bd1d581473e0c1965d70a66654:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"a3d0a4e35ed46af3d0c64